  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/940643f7ff7620d8ecd206cd4035806f021907df</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/940643f7ff7620d8ecd206cd4035806f021907df"/>
    <title>
        fix(coralbricks): DeepSeek V4.1 Flash input $0.30 -&gt; $0.01 on both ID…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-10-11T04:31:49Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1549082?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>opencode-agent</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/opencode-agent</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix(coralbricks): DeepSeek V4.1 Flash input $0.30 -&amp;gt; $0.01 on both IDs (#9344)

CoralBricks cut the DeepSeek V4.1 Flash input rate to $0.01 per 1M tokens,
with a $0.08 cache-write add-on, so a cache-written prompt token still
bills $0.09 in total. Output ($1.20) and free cached reads are unchanged.

deepseek-v4.1-flash-fast and its older alias deepseek-v4.1-flash-fast-fp4
resolve to the same model at the same rates, so update both.

Supersedes #9271, which updated only the -fp4 alias.

Co-authored-by: rekram1-node &amp;lt;rekram1-node@users.noreply.github.com&amp;gt;
Co-authored-by: Divy &amp;lt;divy@coralbricks.ai&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
